<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton rates rise on crop fears.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton rates rise on crop fears.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates rose on Sunday owing to prospects of a short crop, dealers said.</p>
<p>The state-run Cotton Export Corp of Pakistan Ltd said on Saturday that cotton output had reached 8.25 million 375-lb bales by February 13 compared to 9.43 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the kerb market, NIAB-78 was quoted at 2,250 to 2,300 rupees per maund (37.32 kg), one dealer said.  </p>
<p>Sunday's KCA official spot rates in rupees per maund:</p>
<p>				     Sunday	     Feb 15</p>
<p>    NIAB-78			2,333.50	   2,322.50</p>
<p>    K-68			   2,526		2,515</p>
<p>    MNH-93			 2,536		2,525</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
